{% block requirements %}
## REQ-Specific Requirements

### Structure Requirements
1. Requirement Header
2. Atomic Requirements (REQ.XX.YY)
3. Acceptance Criteria
4. Dependencies
5. Verification Matrix

### Requirement Format
```yaml
REQ.XX.YY:
  title: [Short title]
  description: |
    [Detailed requirement statement]
  priority: P0|P1|P2
  category: functional|performance|security|data|interface
  acceptance_criteria:
    - [Criterion 1]
    - [Criterion 2]
  verification:
    method: test|inspection|analysis|demonstration
    test_ref: TSPEC.XX.YY
  trace:
    upstream: SYS.XX.YY
    downstream: SPEC.XX.YY
  status: draft|approved|implemented|verified
```

### Content Quality
- Single atomic requirement
- Clear acceptance criteria
- Testable statements
- Complete traceability
- Status tracking

### ID Pattern
- Format: `REQ.XX.YY` where XX is category, YY is item
- Example: `REQ.03.07` (Third category, seventh requirement)

### Traceability
- @trace: SYS.XX.YY (upstream system requirements)
- Forward references to SPEC/CTR
- Test coverage mapping
{% endblock %}

{% block instructions %}
## REQ Creation Instructions

1. **Decompose System Requirements**
   - Break SYS into atomic units
   - One behavior per requirement
   - Clear boundaries

2. **Define Acceptance Criteria**
   - Measurable conditions
   - Pass/fail determinable
   - Edge cases covered

3. **Assign Verification**
   - Test: Automated/manual testing
   - Inspection: Code review
   - Analysis: Design review
   - Demonstration: User acceptance

4. **Establish Dependencies**
   - Prerequisite requirements
   - Parallel requirements
   - Blocking relationships

5. **Track Status**
   - Draft → Approved → Implemented → Verified
